; The Native4D dialect: a reduced native graph whose tensors occupy only the
; N/H/W/C axes of the six-axis frame. See .ai/native4d_design.md and
; .ai/native4d_plan.md.
;
; WRAPPED, unlike every other library here. The repo convention is `wrapped
; false` so that modules inside a library name each other unqualified — and a
; wrapped `native4d` still names `Vec6`, `Axis`, `Dim`, `Conv`, `Graph_ir`
; unqualified, because those come from `native`, which stays unwrapped. What
; `wrapped false` cannot do is host a SECOND dialect: `include_subdirs
; unqualified` makes every module name globally visible, so a second `Op` /
; `Graph` / `Eval_op` would need a prefix on every file. `Native4d.Op` says the
; same thing with the qualification carrying information.
;
; The consequence to remember: a wrapped library compiles each unit with its
; alias module opened, so a sibling here SHADOWS the same-named module from
; `native`. No file in this directory may be named after one in `lib/native/`
; — hence the `4` suffix on `graph_shape4`, `eval_op4`, `eval_direct4`,
; `eval_symbolic4` and `dialect4`, and only on those.

(library
 (name native4d)
 (libraries core fmt jsont native))
